284c13c690a247e1c7d8434f9c7eb0024d4e641f","event_uuid":"48879d99-d3e3-4e06-b024-12604b09c018","position":{"commit_sha":"0eb15caf142438419a57f98c3151b261ba617dff","position":"1786805177049405001-48879d99-d3e3-4e06-b024-12604b09c018"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cf0a9437eaab8d38e0b5354697c6c44340678f951cb37c016a88fce6bfb33323","event_uuid":"6f9e715e-adda-43e0-bbad-b0abbadadca4","position":{"commit_sha":"9d2cb0a65aa86503439fe0ac44411533637bf998","position":"1786805227115944001-6f9e715e-adda-43e0-bbad-b0abbadadca4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b5c0a82dd0c0fc0d207567721e394d017cffb6e8dbd2c09c9bf6aa86d45ccdd9","event_uuid":"5c98560c-9b5c-47e9-8a81-b4560b8389cb","position":{"commit_sha":"98c70779f13104a784030579d303346f6f8c68f6","position":"1786807387071643001-5c98560c-9b5c-47e9-8a81-b4560b8389cb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (rebar-debug Phase 1, root cause PROVEN + runtime-confirmed):\n\nMECHANISM: story-1734 multi-project fan-out in fetcher._build_snapshot builds one inbound query per key in .bridge_state/projects.json: project_list = list(read_projects().keys()) or [_query_project]. The live tickets branch's projects.json was overwritten with the rehearsal fixture {LEG,ONE,TWO,ZERO / legacy_default:null}; LEG/ONE/TWO/ZERO do not exist in live REB Jira. So the first query jql_active('LEG') = 'project = LEG AND status != \"Done\"' is rejected by Jira (value leg does not exist for field project) -> ACLI exit 1 -> reconcile_once raises -> pass exits 1.\n\nRUNTIME PROOF: (1) CI log run 31887498540 shows the exact failing ACLI command 'project = LEG AND status != \"Done\"'. (2) Local repro: jqls_for('LEG')[0] == 'project = LEG AND status != \"Done\"' (byte-identical). (3) _PROJECT_KEY_RE accepts 'LEG' (syntactically valid) so no validator catches a nonexistent-but-well-formed key.\n\nDISCRIMINATING EVIDENCE (rules out alternatives): first-failure bisect on Reconcile Bridge runs isolates the consistent-failure onset at 2026-08-15T02:39Z; git log of origin/tickets:.bridge_state/projects.json shows commit 9f1b2cff98 ('commit mapping') + 275bd7507e ('scrub'), authored 't <t@t.co>' (the test-fixture git identity), at 2026-08-14T19:18-0700 (=08-15T02:18Z) — 21 min before onset. Not a code regression: the fan-out code is unchanged and correct; the DATA is wrong. The corruption arrived via AD-HOC git commits on the live tickets branch (the exact practice AGENTS.md bans), not via the isolated DC rehearsal harness (which uses random scratch keys + REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off).\n\nLEGITIMACY: defect (production breakage). Authoritative intended state = the ensure-registry seed {version:1, legacy_default:'REB', projects:{}} (project_ensures.seed_projects_mapping_unit), which is also the green-run state (commit 0d9f4b8459). Fix = restore that canonical mapping on origin/tickets.","timestamp":1786805227115944001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"PROJECT INVARIANT (accepted this session): every mutation of the tickets branch MUST (1) be performed under the unified store write lock (rebar._store.lock.write_lock) and (2) auto-commit + auto-publish to sync.remote — the same contract ticket events already honor (docs/concurrency.md 'the store shares every write immediately'). The .bridge_state/projects.json write path (projects_store.set_project/remove_project -> _write_record) VIOLATES both halves: it is a bare tempfile+os.replace with no lock, no commit, and no push. This is the mechanism that forced the ad-hoc hand-commits behind this incident. Follow-up ticket filed to bring bridge-state writes under the locked+committed+published invariant and to codify the invariant in docs/concurrency.md.","timestamp":1786807387071643001}],"created_at":1786805025459226001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"412c67ff-d94b-41e3-9c54-1c76f49dfb21","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336"}],"description":"The scheduled **Reconcile Bridge** GitHub Action (and the Reconciler Heartbeat Canary)\nfails every run on live `navapbc/rebar` since 2026-08-15T02:39Z. ACLI aborts the inbound\nfetch with:\n\n`✗ Error: failed to parse JQL query: the value 'leg' does not exist for the field 'project'`\non JQL `project = LEG AND status != \"Done\"`, so `reconcile_once` raises and the pass exits 1.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe live `tickets` branch's `.bridge_state/projects.json` was overwritten with the\nmulti-project **rehearsal fixture** mapping — keys `LEG`/`ONE`/`TWO`/`ZERO` (repos\n`rebar-legacy`/`rebar`/`rebar-web,rebar-api`/none), `legacy_default: null` — none of which\nexist in the live REB Jira Cloud. The story-1734 multi-project fan-out\n(`fetcher._build_snapshot`: `project_list = list(read_projects().keys()) or [_query_project]`)\nissues `jql_active(proj)` for EVERY mapped key; the first, `project = LEG …`, is\nsyntactically valid (passes `_PROJECT_KEY_RE`) but Jira rejects it because project LEG does\nnot exist → ACLI exit 1 → whole pass fails.\n\nThe corruption landed as ad-hoc `git commit` calls on the live tickets branch\n(`9f1b2cff98` \"commit mapping\" + `275bd7507e` \"scrub\", authored `t <t@t.co>` — the\ntest-fixture git identity) at 2026-08-14T19:18-0700 (=08-15T02:18Z), 21 min before the first\nconsistent failure. The known-good green-run state (commit `0d9f4b8459`) was\n`{legacy_default: \"REB\", projects: {}}` — empty projects → fan-out falls back to the single\nconfigured project REB.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The live `origin/tickets:.bridge_state/projects.json` is restored to the canonical\n  single-project state `{\"version\": 1, \"legacy_default\": \"REB\", \"projects\": {}}` (byte-identical\n  to the ensure-registry seed), removing the nonexistent LEG/ONE/TWO/ZERO keys.\n- [ ] A live `rebar bridge preview` against REB runs without the JQL parse error (no\n  `project = LEG` query is issued) — verified by command output.\n- [ ] The next scheduled Reconcile Bridge run completes green (verified via `gh run view`).\n\n## Testing\n\n- Reproduce the fan-out locally: `python3 -c \"from rebar_reconciler.fetcher import jqls_for; print(jqls_for('LEG'))\"`\n  shows the failing `project = LEG AND status != \"Done\"` query.\n- Verify the repair with `rebar bridge preview` (read-only; no Jira writes) against live REB.\n- Confirm the scheduled `Reconcile Bridge` workflow run goes green.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"d03f98fc-c5ad-43f1-a3bc-5b9a04b12636","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconcile Bridge broken: rehearsal projects.json (LEG/ONE/TWO/ZERO) leaked to live tickets branch","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c980961e-c6b2-4c2e-8997-9955c0a9555c","412c67ff-d94b-41e3-9c54-1c76f49dfb21","57fe87d4-d2ad-4078-9d9d-6e57fac36f67","d03f98fc-c5ad-43f1-a3bc-5b9a04b12636","48879d99-d3e3-4e06-b024-12604b09c018","6f9e715e-adda-43e0-bbad-b0abbadadca4","5c98560c-9b5c-47e9-8a81-b4560b8389cb"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786816266047624001,"uuid":"b2e21c98-0e27-4c38-9390-46c4cfe224a1"}